      "localizations": {}
    },
    "Notification Settings for %@…": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {}
    },
    "Notification history lives in a system database macOS protects, and Full Disk Access is the only permission that can read it. Backglance can’t request it — macOS has no prompt for this one — so the button above opens the setting.": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {}
    },
    "Notification history lives in a system database that macOS protects. There is no narrower permission and no API for it — Full Disk Access is the only way any app can read it. This is also why Backglance is not in the Mac App Store.": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {}
    },
    "Notifications": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {}
    },
    "Notifications from these apps are never stored. Backglance cannot tell which apps are sensitive — add your bank, brokerage or health apps here.": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {}
    },
    "Notifications older than their app's retention window are removed automatically, about every six hours. Pinned notifications are never removed by age.": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {}
    },
    "Notifications that arrive while paused are not archived.": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {}
